{
  "slug": "cover-letter-writing",
  "concept": "Cover Letter Writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "The cover letter is a narrative artifact — a focused, one-page argument for why this human should be in this role at this company. Customization per application is non-negotiable.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The cover letter is a narrative artifact - a focused, one-page argument for why this human should be in this role at this company. Customization per application is non-negotiable.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. The three-part skeleton",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Why this company. Show evidence you've done your homework: a product they shipped, a value they've published.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#1-the-three-part-skeleton",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Why this role. Connect the specific responsibilities to specific skills or experiences you have. Reuse 2-3 keywords from the JD.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#1-the-three-part-skeleton",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Why me. Demonstrate through evidence and stories. Don't list skills; show outcomes.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#1-the-three-part-skeleton",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Opener discipline",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "\"I am writing to apply for the X position at Y.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#2-opener-discipline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "\"My name is X and I am a [degree/title].\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#2-opener-discipline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Stronger openers:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#2-opener-discipline",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "\"I noticed your team published the design for the X system last month - the tradeoffs you made on Y are the same ones I worked through at Z.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#2-opener-discipline",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Show evidence, don't list skills",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Weak: \"I have strong project management skills and am highly organized.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#3-show-evidence-dont-list-skills",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Stronger: \"Last year I shipped the X migration on a six-engineer team. The original estimate was four months; we delivered in five because I caught a dependency that wasn't in the original scope.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#3-show-evidence-dont-list-skills",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Length conventions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "One page maximum, no exceptions.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#4-length-conventions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "250-350 words is the standard target.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#4-length-conventions",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "3-4 short paragraphs, block-formatted.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#4-length-conventions",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Customization per application",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "At a minimum, customize:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#5-customization-per-application",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Company name and the \"why this company\" paragraph",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#5-customization-per-application",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "2-3 keywords from the JD",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#5-customization-per-application",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The job title in the opener",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#5-customization-per-application",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Signature and sign-off",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Salutation: \"Dear [Name],\" when you know the hiring manager's name.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#6-signature-and-sign-off",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Sign-off: \"Sincerely,\" is the universal safe choice.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#6-signature-and-sign-off",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Capitalization: Only the first word of the closing phrase is capitalized.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#6-signature-and-sign-off",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. The \"I\" parade",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Count how many sentences open with \"I.\" If more than half do, the letter reads self-absorbed. Vary openings: lead with the company, the role, the project, the result.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#7-the-i-parade",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The cliché opener. \"I am writing to apply...\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The reused letter. Generic flattery, no company name in the first paragraph.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The skill list. \"Strong communicator, fast learner, team player.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The resume rehash. Repeating the resume's bullets in paragraph form.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The two-page letter. Always cut to one page.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The typo in the company name. Auto-disqualifying.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/cover-letter-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
